    <statement><p>Compute the derivative of the given function.</p>
<p><me>g(t) = 5 t^{5} e^t + 6 \sin t \cos t</me></p>
<p><m>g'(t) =</m><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5t^{4}\mathopen{}\left(5+t\right)e^{t}+6\cos^{2}\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-6\sin^{2}\mathopen{}\left(t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



Use the Product Rule on each term.



<me>\begin{array}{rcl}
    g'(t) \amp =\amp  [(5 t^{5})(e^t) + (25 t^{4})(e^t)]
    + 6 [ (\sin t)(-\sin t) + (\cos t)(\cos t)] \\
    \amp \amp \\
    \amp =\amp  5 t^{4}(5 + t)e^t - 6 \sin^2 t + 6 \cos^2 t
  \end{array}</me>


</solution>
